  "as_of": "2023-06-01",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would update Commonwealth statutory forms, replace outdated disability terminology, correct drafting errors and repeal legislation and provisions that no longer serve a purpose.",
   "Many forms currently prescribed by regulations would instead use prescribed information requirements or approval by ministers and senior officials through publicly registered notifiable instruments.",
   "Language updates would cover family law, social security and veterans' legislation without changing those provisions' meaning, and references to Northern Territory Acts would be modernised."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Nuclear safety inspectors' identity card forms could be approved by the agency head through a notifiable instrument.",
   "Specified security assessment notices could use any format containing the information required by regulations.",
   "An unused regulation-making power specifying media and forms for banks' unclaimed money statements would be repealed."
  ],
  "affected": "Commonwealth administrators, people using statutory forms, regulated businesses and people with disability referred to in the amended laws are affected.",
